## 5. Feature List

### 5.1 Hackathon Build Scope (6 hours — what actually gets built and demoed)

This is a deliberately narrow cut of the original MVP list. Everything here is chosen because it's buildable and demoable in 6 hours by a small team using Cursor/DeepSeek acceleration; anything cut is cut because it isn't, and each cut is explained.

| Feature | Description | Layer |
|---|---|---|
| Seeded medication data | 3 pre-registered medications with name, dosage, instructions, one scheduled time each, and a reference photo taken in advance | Deterministic (seed data, no registration UI) |
| "What do I take now?" query | Voice query resolved against the seeded schedule for the current demo time slot | AI (parsing) + Deterministic |
| Camera-based verification | Match scanned package against the one expected item, using OCR text match and/or barcode against the 3 known references | Computer Vision |
| Three-state confidence output | Match / Mismatch / Uncertain, exposed explicitly | Deterministic |
| Voice output (ElevenLabs) | Speaks the schedule query answer and the verification result, one voice preset per state | Voice |
| Instruction read-aloud | Reads the stored instruction text for the matched medication | Voice (reads stored text only, no generation) |
| Mark as taken | Enabled only after a confirmed match | Deterministic |
| Minimal accessible UI | Large text, high contrast — enough to read on a demo screen, not full WCAG compliance | Flutter |

### 5.2 Cut from the hackathon build (and why)

| Feature | Why it's cut for the 6-hour build |
|---|---|
| Medication registration UI | Seeding 3 medications directly is faster and just as demoable; a registration flow adds UI work with no payoff for a live demo |
