### Reference image capture checklist (do this the day before)
- Photograph each box straight-on, good lighting, plain background, same distance as the phone will realistically be held during the demo.
- Capture the barcode separately if present, and confirm OCR correctly reads the product name from the front label.
- Test the match against a slightly different angle/lighting than the reference photo, since the live demo won't be pixel-identical to the seed image.

### Voice line presets (write these out in advance for ElevenLabs)

**Match:**
> "This is your [medication name]. It matches what's scheduled for now. [Read instruction text]."

**Mismatch:**
> "This doesn't match. You're scheduled for [expected medication], not [scanned item name if identifiable, otherwise 'this']."

**Uncertain:**
> "I'm not sure this matches. Try holding it a bit closer, or check with someone else before taking it."

**Schedule query response:**
> "You need to take your [medication name] now."

Keep the tone flat and calm across all three states — no exclamation points, no urgency-signaling language even in the mismatch case. Panic-coded delivery undermines the "never guess, stay calm" principle the whole product is built on, and it's a detail judges who read the room will notice.
